[{"id":"VRCE-2-5-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":5,"verse":1,"english":"Having given his directions to Rāma as to his in coming installation on the morrow, the king, summoning his priest, Vasiştha spoke to him, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-5-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2005001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6caa5a1e13b35b644e5636a0305004ff6589f1e91470aa40d58e11b27ada879a","compact":"51f4dee025c4645a8f4b34432f5a6a9e0c33495e1ef0765cd6b065ac6851432c","nasal":"51f4dee025c4645a8f4b34432f5a6a9e0c33495e1ef0765cd6b065ac6851432c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-5-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":5,"verse":2,"english":"O you, having asceticism for your wealth, go, to Kākutstha, and for his welfare and obtaining the kingdom, make him fast along with my daughter-in-law.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-5-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2005002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"317ff36b5984f9e702c8421f79f80c95c9ad31fcc562f0238e922610e22f87e4","compact":"01303da23b88becc6dbd964dc55668e262c99166fbc7c126a967f2402e2c6f0a","nasal":"01303da23b88becc6dbd964dc55668e262c99166fbc7c126a967f2402e2c6f0a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-5-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":5,"verse":3,"english":"Thereupon, saying, “So be it,\" that best of those versed in the Veda, the worshipful Vasiştha conversant with mantras, that one practising excellent vows, mounting a Brahma car, himself went to the residence of Rāma cognizant of mantra, for the purpose of making him fast.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-5-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2005003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. D